# Git workflow

__PROJECT_NAME__ follows **Agentic SDD**. The `engineer` plugin skills create
the branches, PRs and tags below; do not create them by hand unless a skill
asks you to.

## Branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| `main` | STAG environment |
| `release` | PROD environment |
| `build/vX.Y.Z.T` | Integration branch of one version, created from `release` |
| `port/vX.Y.Z.T` | Cherry-pick of the build branch onto `main` |

Promotion: PR `port/vX → main` → tag `vX-rc.N` → UAT on STAG → PR
`build/vX → release` → tag `vX`. Pull requests are merged with a **merge
commit**, never squash.

## Versions and tags
`X.Y.Z.T` — X breaking, Y feature, Z improvement, T fix. PROD tags `vX.Y.Z.T`
on `release`; STAG tags `vX.Y.Z.T-rc.N` on `main`. The version lives only in
tags, branch names and `docs/plans/`; not in package manifests.

## Commits — Conventional Commits (mandatory)
`<type>(<scope>)!: <description>` with type in `feat fix perf refactor improve
docs test build ci chore style revert`. `feat` → feature, `fix` → fix,
`perf`/`refactor`/`improve` → improvement, `!` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` → major.
Commits for a WBS goal carry the trailer `Refs: vX.Y.Z.T/G-NN` — a real git
trailer: in the last paragraph, in one block with `Co-Authored-By:` and any
other trailer, no blank line between them. If the repo uses commitlint, its
`type-enum` must allow `improve`.

## Pull requests
Title `<type>: <summary> (vX.Y.Z.T)`. TODO: required reviewers and checks.

## PR checklist
- [ ] Code follows `04-conventions/`
- [ ] No invariant in `02-constraints/invariants.md` is violated
- [ ] If an architectural decision was made, an ADR exists in `03-decisions/`
- [ ] Docs updated if architecture/behavior changed
- [ ] Feature tests and unit tests green (`docs/plans/vX/test-report.md`)
